###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Fine-tuning ran on a single NVIDIA Tesla P100 16 GB GPU and took 14 hours
# on average for MACE and 3 hours for M3GNet with 1402 structures
# (trainingHardware). No inference cost is reported in the parts read.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The surface-energy RMSE column of Table S1 (J/m^2) has no MetricProperty and is not encoded; only the bulk and surface total-energy RMSEs are.
# - Energy RMSEs are printed in eV/atom, for which the vocabulary has no unit; mlips:hasUnit is omitted and the unit is in the label (values are not converted to meV/atom).
# - For the per-element families (NequIP and MTP on [Ong21] and MPtrj*) the paper gives one RMSE over all six elements; the result is linked to all six models, since schema 0.1.2 has no node for a set of models.
# - MTP [Ong21] are the six MTP models published with zuo2020 (registry models model-mtp-<El>-zuo2020), reused here, not refitted.
# - The reference DFT settings are not restated in this paper (Materials Project data and the data of Zuo et al.), so the data sets carry no reference calculation; the [Ong21] settings are in zuo2020.
# - MACE from scratch: '4-body messages in each layer' and 'three hidden layers of 64 hidden units' are not encoded as settings; the fine-tuning runs state only the maximum of 200 epochs (patience 50).
# - The MACE [FT] and M3GNet [FT] models start from the pretrained registry models; schema 0.1.2 cannot express that relation.
# - The universal models were also evaluated on all 1497 Materials Project surfaces of 73 elements; those results are given as figures.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
